From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Count deposits into the guest queue, per message and in total

The trace in events.cpp counts calls to sp_complete. It cannot see what happens
here: a message that fails to land is requeued when its source allows retrying,
and this is the only place a duplicate deposit could be born.

It answered a different question than the one asked, which is the usual way an
instrument earns its keep. The scheduler's interrupt queue saturates: the retrace
message was deposited eight times -- OS_SC_MAX_MESGS -- and then refused, with
refusals being silent drops. That starvation is what delayed the RSP completion
edge past the point where the game had given up on the task.

Two lessons are built into the shape of this trace.

A single global cap lets the most frequent event eat the whole budget: retrace at
sixty per second consumed forty events before the SP edge arrived, and the log
then read "the SP message is never deposited" where it should have read "it has
not been looked at yet". The cap is therefore per message value.

And a cap answers the first seconds while a total answers the whole run. The
per-message cap showed the starvation and then went quiet, exactly when the
remaining question -- is the DP edge refused, and when? -- needed the rest of the
run. Both are kept: first occurrences for the chronology, periodic totals that
cannot be drowned.

Off unless DKR_TRACE_SP is set.

